      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we first need to calculate the perimeter of the original triangle and then determine how many times it would be scaled up to match the perimeter of the neighboring triangle.\n\nPerimeter of the original triangle:\n6 cm + 7 cm + 9 cm = 22 cm\n\nTo find the scale factor, we divide the perimeter of the neighboring triangle by the perimeter of the original triangle:\n\n110 cm / 22 cm = 5\n\nTo find the length of each side of the neighboring triangle, we need to multiply the dimensions of each side of the original triangle by the scale factor:\n\nOriginal:\n6 cm * 5 = 30 cm\n7 cm * 5 = 35 cm\n9 cm * 5 = 45 cm\n\nLongest side length in the neighboring triangle = 45 cm.\n\nThe length of the longest side in the neighboring triangle is 45 centimeters.",
